# gitleaks findings that are not secrets.
#
# gitleaks' generic-api-key rule flags the public fingerprints of the apt
# repository signing keys in the Dockerfile. They are published by MariaDB and
# NodeSource so that anyone can check the keys, and the build compares the
# downloaded keys against them: MARIADB_KEY_FPR (MariaDB's release signing key)
# and NODE_KEY_FPR (NodeSource's repository key).
#
# gitleaks matches a finding by its fingerprint: <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>
# for a scan of the history, and <file>:<rule>:<line> for a scan of the working
# tree. Moving one of these lines in the Dockerfile, or rewriting the commits that
# added them, changes the fingerprint; add the new one here (gitleaks prints it).

